# R21 reveler conversations for the hut costume: logic from tools/content/build_fools_day_dialogue.py, lines drafted by Gemini (R21 revelers), edited.

~ holly_aster_start
holly_aster [smile]: Mind the chimney, mind the eaves, my little house dances and never grieves! Take a hot pie from the windowsill and hop with me, one-two-three, thirty-four, never thirty-five!
-> holly_aster_menu

~ holly_aster_menu
* [if flag.release_slips >= 1] Show them a release slip -> holly_aster_slip
* [Persuasion DC 15] Invite them to a better party, at a quiet church -> holly_aster_church | holly_aster_church_fail
* [Deception DC 15] Say Chuckles wants them at the church for the next number -> holly_aster_church | holly_aster_church_fail
* [knows:calm_emotions] Cast Calm Emotions on them -> holly_aster_calm
* [knows:greater_restoration] Cast Greater Restoration on them -> holly_aster_calm
* Knock them out of the costume, bruised but not hurt for good -> holly_aster_fight
* Leave them dancing for now -> END

~ holly_aster_slip
holly_aster [neutral]: Oh, my poor ankles, and there is pastry grease all over my apron. Where are Violet and Lavender, did Siv get the girls away from the square?
set release_slips -= 1
set reveler_holly_aster = "tickets"
set reveler_holly_aster_freed
set revelers_freed += 1
-> END

~ holly_aster_church
holly_aster [smile]: A grander feast laid out down at the quiet church, lovelies? Wait till I tuck my shutters in, and this old cottage will skip right behind you!
lead holly_aster to fd_silent_church
if check.last
set reveler_holly_aster = "church"
set reveler_holly_aster_freed
set revelers_freed += 1
set church_guests += 1
endif
-> END

~ holly_aster_church_fail
holly_aster [smile]: Go sit in the cold pews when the ovens are roaring and the roofs are kicking up their heels? Stay and dance while we still have nights left to count!
set fd_chuckles_amused
-> holly_aster_menu

~ holly_aster_calm
holly_aster [weary]: My heart is hammering like a trapped bird, and my hands will not stop shaking. I could feel the floorboards of that costume counting down every step I took.
set reveler_holly_aster = "uncharmed"
set reveler_holly_aster_freed
set revelers_freed += 1
-> END

~ holly_aster_fight
holly_aster [angry]: Do not knock upon this manor with sour faces, dears, or the rafters will come down on your heads! Eat your sweetmeats and dance, or the house will trample you flat!
Narrator: The dancers nearby keep on dancing. Nobody here is going to remember a punch.
combat reveler_holly_aster

~ holly_aster_beaten
holly_aster [weary]: Lord above, you have a heavy hand, though it beat spinning until my lungs burst. Help me shed these painted shingles so I can go look for Siv and my girls.
set reveler_holly_aster = "beaten"
set reveler_holly_aster_freed
set revelers_freed += 1
-> END

~ holly_aster_sheltered
holly_aster [weary]: Thirty-four candles I have burned, and for an hour out there I thought I would never bake another loaf. Keep the door shut tight, please, until my fingers stop trembling.
-> END

~ thomasin_ardor_start
thomasin_ardor [smile]: Step right up and mind the hem, my friends, for this whole house was stitched to dance! Come spin with me before the velvet roof comes unstuck!
-> thomasin_ardor_menu

~ thomasin_ardor_menu
* [if flag.release_slips >= 1] Show them a release slip -> thomasin_ardor_slip
* [Persuasion DC 15] Invite them to a better party, at a quiet church -> thomasin_ardor_church | thomasin_ardor_church_fail
* [Deception DC 15] Say Chuckles wants them at the church for the next number -> thomasin_ardor_church | thomasin_ardor_church_fail
* [knows:calm_emotions] Cast Calm Emotions on them -> thomasin_ardor_calm
* [knows:greater_restoration] Cast Greater Restoration on them -> thomasin_ardor_calm
* Knock them out of the costume, bruised but not hurt for good -> thomasin_ardor_fight
* Leave them dancing for now -> END

~ thomasin_ardor_slip
thomasin_ardor [neutral]: Oh, my knees are trembling like loose basting thread. How long had I been prancing about in this dreadful painted timber and canvas?
set release_slips -= 1
set reveler_thomasin_ardor = "tickets"
set reveler_thomasin_ardor_freed
set revelers_freed += 1
-> END

~ thomasin_ardor_church
thomasin_ardor [smile]: A quiet gathering with fine new garments to admire sounds simply lovely! Lead the way, and mind my chicken-leg boots on the cobbles!
lead thomasin_ardor to fd_silent_church
if check.last
set reveler_thomasin_ardor = "church"
set reveler_thomasin_ardor_freed
set revelers_freed += 1
set church_guests += 1
endif
-> END

~ thomasin_ardor_church_fail
thomasin_ardor [smile]: Sit still in a dusty pew when the ribbons are flying so merrily? Never, my dears, this manor has seven more reels to dance!
set fd_chuckles_amused
-> thomasin_ardor_menu

~ thomasin_ardor_calm
thomasin_ardor [weary]: The music finally stopped pulling at my heels, thank goodness. Whoever stitched this coarse canvas house had no eye for proper seams at all.
set reveler_thomasin_ardor = "uncharmed"
set reveler_thomasin_ardor_freed
set revelers_freed += 1
-> END

~ thomasin_ardor_fight
thomasin_ardor [angry]: Do not tug at the tapestry, friends, or the manor will have to trample you flat! Nobody ruins the grand pattern tonight!
Narrator: The dancers nearby keep on dancing. Nobody here is going to remember a punch.
combat reveler_thomasin_ardor

~ thomasin_ardor_beaten
thomasin_ardor [weary]: You might have spared the pleated eaves, though I suppose I deserved a sharp tap. At least you knocked this wretched framework off my shoulders.
set reveler_thomasin_ardor = "beaten"
set reveler_thomasin_ardor_freed
set revelers_freed += 1
-> END

~ thomasin_ardor_sheltered
thomasin_ardor [weary]: It is mercifully still in here, though my ankles ache from those wooden stilts. I remember smiling while my feet bled, and I could not stop.
-> END

